      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Litchfield%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Before settling on Litchfield, the village was known as Round Lake, Ripley, and later Ness.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Litchfield%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The first train to arrive in Litchfield was a construction train on August 13, 1869.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Litchfield%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The railroad erected a 25‑by‑60‑foot building called an immigrant’s reception house to welcome newcomers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Litchfield%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Trinity Episcopal Church, founded in 1871, earned a spot on the National Register of Historic Places in 1975.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
